# Coffee-edge

- Project root is this Track 2 folder. Dataset samples live in `data/_sample/`.
- Paths come from `config/config.yaml`, `COFFEE_*` env vars, or CLI flags. Do not hard-code data, model, or output paths.
- Docker bind mount is only `${HOST_DATA_DIR}` -> `/data`. Switching dataset means editing `.env`.
- Class folders, in id order: `good`, `shell`, `full_black`, `hull_husk`, `broken`, `parchment`, `immature`.
- The only label format is YOLO segmentation polygon text (`labels.format: yolo_seg_txt`).
- Pi runtime image: Python, numpy, opencv-python-headless, ncnn, pyyaml. No PyTorch, ultralytics, or scikit-learn.
- No camera input. Sources are an image file or a folder.
- `day` is 1, 2, or 3. Do not hard-code class counts, image names, or folder populations.
- YOLO26 NCNN output names and shapes are written only after a real export is inspected.
- Use logging. Do not swallow exceptions.
